00:00:13.661 --> 00:00:15.770
- (laughs) why are you
so far, do we scare you?

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:16.704
- I know hey?

00:00:16.704 --> 00:00:17.537
- Of course you do.

00:00:17.537 --> 00:00:18.820
- Like you guys talk, I'll be...

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.940
- I know he grew up in
Wales, but you grew up here--

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.030
- I grew up in Brooklyn so yeah.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.300
- You grew up watching Mr Rogers.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.952
- Yeah, yeah I did, absolutely.

00:00:25.952 --> 00:00:26.785
- (Audience member) Brooklyn!

00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:27.618
- I like it, okay.

00:00:27.618 --> 00:00:28.540
- Brooklyn is always in the house, yep.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.559
- I love it.

00:00:29.559 --> 00:00:30.392
And you watched it as a kid?

00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:33.070
- Yeah, my brother and I,
we watched it all the time.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.940
I mean, I joke around but, I was like,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.670
was I preparing for this
since I'm five years old?

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.240
Like I remember, just all of it

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.470
and it's all attached to like
a really sweet time in life

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.602
where you didn't know
much about anything yet.

00:00:44.602 --> 00:00:45.435
- Mhm.

00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:50.010
- And he was sort of your
entry way into so much of like,

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.060
what is is to think about your feelings

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:52.933
or what it is to like-

00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:53.766
- Life.

00:00:53.766 --> 00:00:55.660
- Yeah, explore life in this really calm,

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.390
sort of, patient way.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.890
- [Kelly] Yeah, so, who do you play?

00:00:58.890 --> 00:00:59.810
What's your role in the movie?

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:00.643
Tell everyone.

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:01.960
- I play Andrea.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.605
I'm his ball and chain.

00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:06.540
And our relationship is this-

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.970
Its in a complicated place,

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.230
you know , I think with relationships,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.930
you know, there's sometimes
these points where there's just

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.740
miscommunication and we're
just missing each other.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.870
Like, we're both on two
different pages at the moment

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:16.830
and we're trying to get realigned.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.170
- Especially when you bring kids in.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.003
- Exactly.

00:01:19.003 --> 00:01:20.210
And so now we have a newborn

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.890
and we're trying to get realigned

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.460
and it's not quite happening.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.750
- I loved y'all.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.800
Like, on screen together.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.660
It was so well done, like
all the hurt, the laughing,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.493
all of it.

00:01:29.493 --> 00:01:32.040
It was just like, so well played out

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.560
to how actual relationships-

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:34.393
- Oh, good.

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.226
- How we interact with each other.

00:01:35.226 --> 00:01:36.059
It was really good.

00:01:36.059 --> 00:01:38.930
But you, you actually
have a really good, like,

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:40.520
neighbor story, like growing up, right?

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.620
Like, when you had your
land lady I heard about?

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:43.453
- Oh yeah!

00:01:43.453 --> 00:01:44.286
You know what?

00:01:44.286 --> 00:01:45.390
My land lady, bless her heart

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.330
and bless people who are like this.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.300
I was so broke and just
trying to be an artist

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.580
and trying to stay true to my art

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:54.520
and my land lady in Brooklyn, Fredrica.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:55.730
She'll love this.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.170
She's an artist and she basically let me

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.710
stay in my apartment
because I was an artist.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.850
And I called her one day, I said,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.920
Look, I really can't afford
to be here, you know,

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.610
and I don't wanna hold
you up and I don't wanna

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:08.800
feel like I owe you.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.750
So, Ill leave and I just
wanted to give you some notice.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:13.990
She said, look, just stay.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.280
I know what you're trying to do,

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.010
I know where you're trying to go in life.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.260
Forget any late fees, forget,
like, any paying on time,

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.050
just when you can get it to me, get it.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.000
You're a good tenent.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.240
I'd rather just see you try and succeed

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.660
and you can stay in the place.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.048
Isn't' that something?

00:02:28.048 --> 00:02:30.215
- So remarkable!
- Amazing!

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:34.159
- Usually the land lady and
they're knocking on the door

00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:35.947
I know you're hiding in there.

00:02:35.947 --> 00:02:36.860
- Right, right, exactly!

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:37.857
- Yes, yes!

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.378
I mean not that I've done that.

00:02:39.378 --> 00:02:40.831
(nervous laugh)

00:02:40.831 --> 00:02:42.860
- And this is in Brooklyn
where prices are sky rocketing

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.610
and you can get anyone to come in

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.840
and pay double what I'm paying

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.950
and she just really invested in me

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.150
and that kind of thing,
you know, gets passed on

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:51.983
in some way.

00:02:51.983 --> 00:02:52.816
I hope to do that for someone.

00:02:52.816 --> 00:02:54.377
- I heard about that
story and I was just like,

00:02:54.377 --> 00:02:55.440
"What a beautiful way."

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.090
and then you to take
that and pay it forward

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:57.923
for someone one day.

00:02:57.923 --> 00:02:58.756
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:58.756 --> 00:03:00.480
- Its a beautiful
neighborhood kind of vibe.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.429
- Very much so.

00:03:01.429 --> 00:03:02.262
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:03:02.262 --> 00:03:03.095
- Very much so.

00:03:03.095 --> 00:03:03.928
- Did you get, I'm asking everyone.

00:03:03.928 --> 00:03:06.330
